From: Ghaf contributors <ghaf@tii.ae>
Subject: [PATCH] dce: bound the client IPC wait for a DCE reply

dce_client_ipc_wait() blocks until the R5 raises the client's completion, and
restarts the wait whenever a signal interrupts it. A wedged R5 therefore holds
the caller in tegra_dce_client_ipc_send_recv() for good, even against SIGKILL.
For the host dce-host proxy that caller is a VMM thread inside write(), which
cannot be killed, so the VMM and its guest can never be stopped.

Give up after 10 s and return -ETIMEDOUT. The wait is no longer interruptible:
interruption only ever restarted it, and with a fatal signal pending the
restart would spin until the deadline. 10 s is far above the latency expected
of a display RPC while staying well inside the hung-task and systemd stop
timeouts.

Host only. The guest short-circuits dce_ipc_send_message_sync() through
tegra_dce_ipc_send_redirect (0001) before it can reach this wait.
---
--- a/drivers/platform/tegra/dce/dce-client-ipc.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/tegra/dce/dce-client-ipc.c
@@ -266,6 +266,12 @@
 	destroy_workqueue(d_aipc->async_event_wq);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Upper bound on how long a client RPC waits for the R5 to answer. A wedged R5
+ * would otherwise hold the caller here for good.
+ */
+#define DCE_CLIENT_IPC_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS	(10U * 1000)
+
 int dce_client_ipc_wait(struct tegra_dce *d, u32 int_type)
 {
 	uint32_t type;
@@ -285,11 +291,17 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-retry_wait:
-	DCE_COND_WAIT_INTERRUPTIBLE(&cl->recv_wait,
-			atomic_read(&cl->complete) == 1);
-	if (atomic_read(&cl->complete) != 1)
-		goto retry_wait;
+	/*
+	 * Not interruptible: signals only restarted the wait, and with one
+	 * pending the restart would spin until the deadline.
+	 */
+	if (!wait_event_timeout(cl->recv_wait.wq,
+				atomic_read(&cl->complete) == 1,
+				msecs_to_jiffies(DCE_CLIENT_IPC_WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS))) {
+		dce_err(d, "Timed out waiting for DCE reply on int_type: [%d]",
+			int_type);
+		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	}
 
 	atomic_set(&cl->complete, 0);
 
